:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Docs",
    title: "Haml And Markdown",
    summary: "Haml and Markdown modules compile to Ruby component classes while leaving rendering policy to the consuming application."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "HamlPlugin" }
    :markdown
      `HamlPlugin` is an adapter, not a renderer. The application supplies a component base class and an HTML/component factory.

      ```ruby
      Klenod::Build::Plugins::HamlPlugin.new(
        component_base_class: "App::Component",
        factory: "App::H"
      )
      ```

      Haml files transform into Ruby component classes exported as `Default`. Importing Haml from Ruby or Haml returns that component class.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Haml Features" }
    :markdown
      Haml modules support imports, component references such as `%Card`, Ruby filters, inline CSS filters, and `:markdown` filters.

      Companion files are tracked automatically:

      - `Component.css` is imported as `Styles` when present.
      - `Component.intl.*.toml` files are watched and exposed as translations.
      - Adding, editing, or removing companions invalidates the owning Haml module.

      Generated Ruby includes source map marks so runtime errors can be rewritten back to original Haml source lines.

  %DocsSection{ title: "MarkdownPlugin" }
    :markdown
      `MarkdownPlugin` handles `.md` modules and Haml `:markdown` filters through `kramdown` with the GFM parser.

      ```ruby
      Article = import("./article.md")
      ```

      Markdown files transform into Ruby component classes exported as `Default`. Markdown renders elements as factory calls rather than raw HTML strings, including raw HTML elements in the Markdown source.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Markdown Components" }
    :markdown
      If `/markdown-components.rb` exists, Markdown rendering uses its `Default` hash to map tags to components.

      ```ruby
      Heading = import("/components/MarkdownHeading.haml")
      Link = import("/components/MarkdownLink.haml")

      Default = {
        h1: Heading,
        a: Link
      }.freeze
      ```

      Unmapped tags fall back to symbol tags such as `:p`, `:a`, and `:code`.
